  "understandChart": "Understand your chart",
  "guideEyebrow": "A LITTLE WISDOM, A LOT OF POSSIBILITY",
  "guideTitle": "Ancient roots.\nHuman connections.",
  "guideIntro": "BaZi is a traditional Chinese system for exploring the patterns of a birth moment. FatePair brings that tradition into a more curious, connected world.",
  "meetElements": "Meet the Five Elements",
  "elementsTagline": "Different by nature. Better in balance.",
  "guidePillarsTitle": "What are the Four Pillars?",
  "guidePillarsBody": "Your birth year, month, day, and hour each form a pillar. Each pillar has a heavenly stem and an earthly branch — eight characters in total. That is what BaZi means: “eight characters.” Your day stem is called your day master.",
  "guideHarmonyTitle": "How does FatePair calculate harmony?",
  "guideHarmonyBody": "Our demo score combines three transparent factors: 45% combined element balance, measured by the normalized entropy of visible elements; 35% day master connection, based on the generating cycle; and 20% day branch resonance, using traditional pairs, trines, and oppositions. Scores are computed from the charts and recommendations are sorted from highest to lowest.",
  "guideScoreTitle": "What does a high score mean?",
  "guideScoreBody": "It means two charts align under our chosen rules. These rules are an interpretive product choice, not a scientific test of personality or relationship success. A score should invite a conversation, never decide who deserves one. Shared values, kindness, consent, and real-life chemistry matter.",
  "guideTimezoneTitle": "How do time zones work?",
  "guideTimezoneBody": "FatePair resolves your birth time using the IANA time-zone database, including historical daylight saving rules. Year and month use the calendar library’s solar-term instants in UTC+8. Dating recommendations use local mean solar time based on birthplace longitude, with the day changing at midnight. Chart Studio additionally supports local clock time, true solar time with an approximate equation-of-time correction, and a 23:00 day boundary. During a repeated clock-change time, the earlier occurrence is used; nonexistent clock-change times are rejected. Other BaZi schools may produce different charts.",
  "guideNoTimeTitle": "What if I don’t know my birth time?",
  "guideNoTimeBody": "You can still explore. FatePair uses local noon for the date calculation, omits the hour pillar, and marks your results as approximate. On dates near a solar-term boundary, year or month may be uncertain too. Add your time later to refine your chart.",
  "guideCommunityTitle": "Is this a live dating community?",
  "guideCommunityBody": "This first version is an interactive, local demo. The people shown are fictional profiles paired with stock photographs. You can explore charts, filter recommendations, and save connections on this device. Accounts, messages, verification, and a real community will be part of a future backend integration.",
